# Celery falls back to the task-level limit when a delivery is recovered or
# redelivered without its per-message timelimit header.  Keep that fallback at
# least as large as the longest normal control-stage budget; otherwise a
# PRODUCTION_PLAN/DIRECTOR delivery can be killed at the legacy generic limit
# even though its durable stage lease and published budget both authorize a
# longer run.  Normal publishes still carry the exact per-stage limits from
# ``_stamp_stage_execution_budget``.
